{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966795,"nonce":"QZw3t2nj2Bgr4zaHQVD+QM3JmxQ=","title":"Every kit.hit_rect call clones the entire SpatialIndex via State::update — O(R²) clone","message":"`CanvasKit::hit_rect` (packages/blinc_canvas_kit/src/lib.rs around\nline 454) routes through `State\u003cSpatialIndex\u003e::update()`. The\nreactive `State::update` semantics\n(`crates/blinc_core/src/reactive.rs:283-310`) are:\nget_untracked → CLONE the whole `T` → run the closure on the clone\n→ `set` back → `notify_stateful_deps` + `notify_property_bindings`\n+ `notify_portals` + `drain_deferred_writes`.\n\nFor SpatialIndex, T contains a `HashMap\u003c(i32, i32), Vec\u003cusize\u003e\u003e` +\na `Vec\u003cHitRegion\u003e`. The clone is the full data structure. Each\nhit_rect call sees an index that already includes prior frame's\ninserts → costs grow as the frame progresses → total work per\npaint is approximately `Σ(i for i in 0..R)` = **O(R²/2)** byte\nclones, plus 17k notify-tree walks.\n\n**Workflow finding (2026-06-20)**: on a 500-node / 1000-edge graph\nthe call counts per paint are:\n- ~5–9 group hit_rects per group (body, badge, title, desc,\n  collapse/edit/delete chrome). NOT frustum-gated.\n- ~8 segment_bboxes per visible edge (each is a separate hit_rect).\n- ~3–10 per visible node (body, badge, per-port).\n- ≈ 17,000 hit_rect calls per paint at typical graph sizes.\n\nThis is the **dominant source of zoom-jank** that scales with TOTAL\nnode count regardless of how many nodes are visible. It is NOT a\nGPU problem; it is a CPU-side reactive-state issue.\n\n**Why a naive GPU cull regressed it (the false-trail attempt)**:\nThe node-editor already pre-frustum-culls at `editor.rs:4173`\nbefore emitting primitives. Adding `cull_primitives` to\n`render_primitives_overlay` had ~0% rejection rate → pure overhead\nfrom a `Vec\u003cGpuPrimitive\u003e::collect()` per call (~720KB/frame on a\nbig graph). The GPU cull lane was wrong; the cost is upstream of\nGPU dispatch.\n\n**Cheapest correct fix paths (pick one)**:\n\n1. **Batch hit_rect into a frame-local Vec**, commit once at\n   frame-end. Each call appends to a `Vec\u003cHitRegion\u003e` (push, no\n   clone). At end of frame, one `State::update` swaps in the new\n   collection. Reduces 17k clones → 1.\n\n2. **Move SpatialIndex out of `State\u003cT\u003e` reactive storage**, into\n   `Arc\u003cRwLock\u003cSpatialIndex\u003e\u003e` directly on `CanvasKit`. hit_rect\n   becomes a write-lock + insert. No clone, no notify cascade.\n   Lose the reactive-subscription side (nothing depends on\n   SpatialIndex changing per insert anyway — the kit only reads\n   it for hit-test from its own non-reactive paths).\n\n3. **Defer hit_rect updates** until interaction state actually\n   needs them. Most paints don't immediately hit-test the new\n   regions — the hit-test happens on the NEXT pointer event.\n\nApproach #2 is the cleanest architectural fix.\n\n**Secondary contributors** flagged by the same workflow lane:\n\n- `nested_body_growth` (editor.rs:3378-3425): O(G²) double loop +\n  HashMap/HashSet clones per group. Result is invariant under\n  camera moves — should be cached by `(graph_rev, theme_rev)`.\n- `preliminary_bodies` (editor.rs:3348-3377): O(G·N)\n  `node_bounds_for` calls, each with RwLock read + Mutex lock +\n  fingerprint hash. Same memoisation opportunity.\n- Group draw loop redoes the same `compute_group_auto_bounds` +\n  `node_bounds_for` work a SECOND time per paint (L3442-3517).\n- Frustum cull runs AFTER the heavy O(N) sweeps — off-frustum\n  nodes pay the prepass cost even when culled.\n\n**Companion notes**:\n\n- Portal::frame overhead (~7-10 Mutex acquisitions per portal per\n  frame, `kit.interaction()` subscribing every portal to\n  mousemove spam, `consumed_height` drift firing\n  `blinc_layout::request_redraw` per node per frame) is the\n  second tier of cost. Address after hit_rect.\n- Web amplification: unconditional rAF self-perpetuating loop\n  (`crates/blinc_animation/src/scheduler.rs:756-781`) reschedules\n  without checking `has_active`/`needs_redraw`.\n  `CanvasViewport::update → notify_stateful_deps → HUD signal →\n  queue_subtree_rebuild → invalidate_render_cache_tagged\n  ('subtree_rebuild_applied')` fires every wheel tick.\n- Full workflow output at\n  `/private/tmp/.../tasks/wl60vuity.output`.","files":null}]}